== Layout baselines: the three re-captured in T46 (fc03e39) against the ones recorded from main ==
The baselines did not exist at 72cf58b (`git show 72cf58b:tests/e2e/editor-layout.spec.ts-snapshots/...` is empty). They were first recorded from main's app (72cf58b) in d40c9aa
("masked Linux baselines from main", tests/e2e/README.md), so d40c9aa is the "old" image. "New" is HEAD (re-taken in fc03e39). Old, new and diff images (Playwright's own
comparator, red = differing pixels) are outside the repo, in the job's scratch directory: baseline-review/<name>.{old,new,diff}.png.
- editor-new-invoice-desktop-chromium-linux.png: 35% of pixels differ.
  Editor column: the new invoice now opens with the default sender profile and bank account filled in (T22), so "Test Sender Profile" and "Test Bank (USD)" are chosen
  and their detail cards show; everything below moves down about 220 px. Preview column: it was fully masked; now only the preview's header and sender/bill-to blocks are masked,
  so the empty items table, the $0.00 subtotal and total and the payment block are compared. The preview now shows the red "The logo link is not a secure web address.
  The PDF was made without it." notice (the seeded sender's logo is http), as the existing-invoice baseline already did. The cookie banner is now fully visible (in the old
  image the masked date fields were drawn over it).
- editor-new-invoice-phone-chromium-linux.png: 9% differ. Same cause as the desktop editor column: sender and bank are pre-filled with their cards, so "To" moves down
  and "Invoice Details" (with its masked invoice number) falls below the fold. Header, cookie banner and Accept button are unchanged.
- editor-existing-invoice-desktop-chromium-linux.png: 26% differ, all in the preview column. The editor column and header are pixel-identical. Only the narrower preview mask
  changed: the preview's table (Test Item, $100.00, 1 pcs, $100.00), subtotal, total and payment information are now visible and compared, and the right part of the
  cookie banner (with the Accept button) that the old full mask covered.
- editor-existing-invoice-phone-chromium-linux.png was not re-taken; it is byte-identical to d40c9aa.
No change is in the editor layout itself: every difference comes from the pre-filled sender/bank of T22 or from the narrower preview mask of T46.

